<BaseLayout
  title="Runr Influencers - In-House Creator Network & Brand Collaborations"
  description="Meet Runr's in-house influencer tribe and explore cross-brand collaborations - real creators, matched to brands by genuine fit, not follower count."
  keywords="influencer marketing agency India, in-house influencer network, entrepreneur collaboration agency, brand collaboration agency Gujarat"
  canonical="https://www.runr.in/influencers/"
  page="influencers"
  pagename="Influencers"
  slider={false}
  swiperjs={false}
  counter={false}
  onepagemenu={true}
>


  <section
    id="section-influencers"
    class="section section-influencers theme-padding pb-0"
  >
  
    <div class="columns is-multiline is-vcentered">
      <div
        class="column is-12-mobile is-12-tablet is-6-desktop is-6-widescreen js-scroll fade-in-left scrolled"
      >
        <div class="section-title title-animate">
          <span class="sub-title">Our Tribe</span>
          <h1 class="text-xl text-uppercase"
            >Creative <span class="theme-text">Voices</span>
          </h1>
          <div class="influencers-content mt-4">
            <p>
            A dynamic community of creators, storytellers, and trendsetters who shape conversations, inspire audiences, and bring fresh ideas to life across digital platforms. What makes this tribe different isn't reach - plenty of accounts have reach. It's that every person here has an audience that actually listens to them, which is a much harder thing to fake, buy, or automate.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div
        class="column is-12-mobile is-12-tablet is-6-desktop is-6-widescreen js-scroll fade-in-right scrolled"
      >
        <div class="influencers-img">
          <picture>
            <img
              src="/media/images/home/influencers/influncers-img.webp"
              alt="Influencers Image"
            />
          </picture>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-influencers-grid theme-padding">
  <div class="section-title title-animate has-text-centered">
  <span class="sub-title">The</span>
    <h2 class="text-xl text-uppercase"> Runr <span class="theme-text">Tribe</span></h2>
  </div>
  <div class="influencers-content mb-6 has-text-centered js-scroll fade-in-bottom scrolled">
    <p>Why we built an in-house tribe instead of just brokering deals - most influencer marketing agencies are middlemen who connect you to creators they don't really know. We built our own roster instead, so when we tell a brand "this creator is right for you," it's based on years of actually working together, not a media kit.</p>
  </div>
  
    <div class="columns is-mobile is-multiline is-justify-content-center influencers-cols gap-1">
      {
        influencers.map((item, index) => (
          <div
            class="column is-6-mobile is-4-tablet is-4-desktop is-3-widescreen influencers-col"
            data-index={index}
          >
            <div class="theme-block pb-0">
              <div class="theme-block-img">
                <div class="theme-block-element">
                  <img
                    loading="lazy"
                    src={`/media/images/home/influencers/${item.layer}`}
                    width="370"
                    height="250"
                    alt="Element"
                  />
                </div>
                <picture class="influencers-img">
                  <img
                    loading="lazy"
                    src={`/media/images/home/influencers/${item.photo}`}
                    width="600"
                    height="400"
                    alt={item.name}
                  />
                </picture>
              </div>
              <div class="theme-block-title">
                <h5><span class="influencer-name-wrap"><span class="txt">{item.name}</span></span></h5>
              </div>
              <div class="influencer-social">
                {item.instagram && (
                  <a
                    href={item.instagram}
                    target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer"
